name: Dependency inventory updates Components, keeps honest failures and recovers without discovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI VIZ | initial-gallery
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 25 Component inventory failed | initial-failure
expect: run sbom-scan:scan
ask: Is the failed dependency inventory reachable with a concrete rerun command, without presenting old package data or phase completion?
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART repair
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | repair-origin
submit: run sbom-scan:scan
require-live-snap: 35 sbom-scan: 2 components | inventory-produced
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 25 COMPONENT STACK | repaired-components
expect: owned-library
expect: declared ^1.0
expect: 1.2.3
expect: Source freshness is unverified
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART repaired
ask: Does the actual tool result repair the cached failure and distinguish the declared constraint from observed lockfile versions without claiming current source freshness?
keys: Escape
expect-echo-within: 300 dependency-draft
live-snap: preserved-draft
nav-mode:
keys: C-_
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART revise
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | revised-origin
submit: run sbom-scan:scan
require-live-snap: 35 sbom-scan: 2 components | revised-inventory-produced
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 25 declared ^2.0 | revised-components
expect: 2.2.3
expect-not: declared ^1.0
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART revised
resize: 160x48
live-snap: components-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: components-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: components-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: components-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: components-40x12
expect: PgUp/PgDn page
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-1-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-2-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-3-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-4-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-5-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-6-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-7-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: components-page-8-40x12
expect: COMPONENTS
expect: q back
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART pages
ask: Are the inventory receipt, source-freshness limitation, manifest constraints and lockfile versions readable through keyboard paging across six terminal sizes?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART corrupt
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | failed-origin
submit: run sbom-scan:scan
require-live-snap: 35 parse package.json | failed-run
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 25 Component inventory failed | failed-components
expect: run sbom-scan:scan
expect-not: owned-library
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
keys: g
resize: 40x12
live-snap: failure-40x12
expect: PgUp/PgDn page
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-1-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-2-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-3-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-4-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-5-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-6-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failure-pages
expect: Esc dismiss
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 15 COMPONENTS | failure-notice-dismissed
expect-not: Esc dismiss
resize: 120x36
ask: Does a real failed rerun clear current package claims while retaining previous successful receipts and a visible recovery action?
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART repair
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | recovery-origin
submit: run sbom-scan:scan
require-live-snap: 35 sbom-scan: 2 components | recovered-run
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 25 declared ^1.0 | recovered-components
expect: 1.2.3
expect-not: declared ^2.0
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI VIZ | restarted-gallery
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 25 declared ^1.0 | restarted-components
expect: 1.2.3
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_inventory.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart read the repaired repository again and retain all run receipts without provider calls, discovery jobs, source execution or manufactured workflow completion?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
